/security-review — R7 round 3 — range 55be3bed..645bb0e5 (fix delta 75463772..645bb0e5 examined)

NO FINDINGS — `landedGlob` runs only over paths `filesUnder(config)` yields, matched as `relative(config, …)`, and the absolute/`..` refusal still returns before it; so no pack glob can turn into a read outside `config/`. The regex is fully anchored (`^…$`), every metacharacter except `*`/`?` is escaped before the wildcard substitution, `*`→`[^/]*` and `?`→`[^/]` stay in-segment, and `**`→`(?:[^/]+/)*` cannot cross a segment boundary into a false match (its only defect is a trailing `**` matching nothing — a false "no match", i.e. a stricter checker, not a false resolve). The `secrets: none` refusal only tightens. Payload edits: taplo `exclude` is order-independent and its entries are byte-identical; the pre-commit `description` is a folded plain scalar whose text is unchanged, and no `exclude`/`entry` line moved.
